rif; font-size:10.5pt\">Good day.</span></p><p style=\"margin:0; margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"color:#1A1A1A; font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif; font-size:10.5pt\">My Name is Neeraj and I'm from Microsoft Azure backup Team.</span></p><p style=\"margin:0; margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"color:#1A1A1A; font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif; font-size:10.5pt\">Thank you for the detailed report and for sharing the steps and the Managed HSM RBAC configuration on case <b>2607290030001963</b>. I have completed an initial analysis of the Confidential VM backup validation failure (<i>&quot;Azure Backup could not get access to key vault / managed HSM associated with some of the selected confidential VM(s)&quot;</i>) for VM <b>cvm-test-rhel-app</b>.</span></p><h3 style=\"margin-bottom:3.0pt; margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"color:#00AA55; font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif; font-size:13.5pt\"><strong>Most important finding</strong></span></h3><p style=\"margin:0; margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in\"><span style=\"color:#1A1A1A; font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif; font-size:10.5pt\"><b>The Managed HSM RBAC you configured is actually correct — it is not the cause.</b> You assigned the built-in role <b>Managed HSM Crypto User</b> to <b>Backup Management Service</b> at scope&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color:#1A1A1A; font-family:Gulim,sans-serif; font-size:12pt\"><code style=\"font-family:GulimChe\">/</code></span><span style=\"color:#1A1A1A; font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif; font-size:10.5pt\">. I verified against the Managed HSM built-in-roles matrix that this role already grants <b>both</b> data actions Azure Backup requires for a Confidential VM:</span></p><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li class=\"x_x_ck-list-marker-font-size x_x_ck-list-marker-color x_x_ck-list-marker-font-family\" data-list-item-id=\"e415f8c729ebd4376821c8475931b68e3\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in; margin-right